\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Breathe of God, breathe on us now,
\par And move within us while we pray;
\par The spring of our new life art Thou,
\par The very light of our new day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O strangely art Thou with us, Lord,
\par Neither in height nor depth to seek:
\par In nearness shall Thy voice be heard;
\par Spirit to spirit  Thou dost speak.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Christ our Advocate on high;
\par Thou art our Advocate within:
\par O pledge the truth, and make reply
\par To every argument of sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. But ah, this faithless heart of mine!
\par The way I know; I know my guide:
\par Forgive me, O my Friend divine,
\par That I so often turn aside.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Be with me when no other friend 
\par The mystery of my heart can share;
\par And be Thou known, when fears transcend, 
\par By Thy best name of Comforter.
\par \tab Amen,\f1 
\par \pard 
\par }

